-bridge only: old clients cannot erase the child document by their whole-document
-`set` (`app/js/gate.js:291`). Canonical state stores `legacyAppliedAt`; new client
-imports legacy state only when its `updatedAt` is later, normalises it, then
-advances that marker. This makes an old client's later legacy write observable
-without allowing it to destroy record clocks/tombstones. New clients never use
-legacy state as canonical after migration.
+Merge unionizes ids within a kind and chooses greater envelope clock; it raises
+the device HLC from every received envelope. Notes/reports: per question-id LWW.
+`scheduleDay[date]` `{date,rest}`: LWW. `scheduleItem[id]`
+`{id,date,label,text,hex}`: LWW, including label. Render live sorted days/items;
+a deleted day hides live items. `sched[date+'|'+itemId]`: one mark LWW. Item id
+is `deviceId+'-'+issue()[0]+'-'+issue()[1]`, never index. Delete item plus marks;
+delete day plus currently known items/marks. Never renumber.
 
