+day/item, notes, profiles, and every other kind writes `del:true`. Retain all
+tombstones one year from winning clock. GC only during successful authenticated
+v1 transaction after remote/local merge; never offline/local-only. Remove only
+expired tombstones from both canonical copies, atomically.
 
-Pin exact, versioned Firebase CDN URLs and SHA-384 `integrity` values in the
-`SDK` list; set `crossOrigin='anonymous'` before append. Preserve `loadSDK()`'s
-8 s timeout and `boot()` 15 s race/local-only fallback.
+When `lastSeenOnlineAt` is over one year old, local v1 cache is stale: pull,
+validate, merge, then permit push. For an active local record older than horizon
+and absent remotely, suppress it (remote absence wins only in this stale rule),
+save, then push. This avoids normal stale resurrection after GC but drops such
+stale unsynced edits. Residual risk: a >1-year-offline old client, manual
+restore/import, or stopped stale-repull can resurrect a GC'd delete. Block
+automatic push in those conditions and require reconnect before syncing.
+
+## Validation, migration, ownership
+
+Extract `parseProgressState(raw)`: JSON parse then `checkedProgressState`.
+Import and every cloud read call it; extend validator for v1 envelopes, stable
+ids and roster fields. Invalid cloud data is not merged/written; show retryable
+error. Preserve actual `loadState` missing/unparseable/invalid rescue.
 
-## Migration and compatibility
+First v1 load converts materialised state without loss. Per entry, seed clock
+from best existing timestamp: value `at` where present (`answers`, `notes`,
+etc.), else relevant `updatedAt`; schedule uses containing state `updatedAt`.
+Use `[timestamp,0,deviceId]`, never migration time. Assign legacy schedule item
+ids and translate `date|index` marks in one atomic local save. Save `syncV` only
+with helpers/envelopes: interrupted pre-save restarts; post-save is idempotent.
+
+If changed legacy `state` appears, validate and import only its present entries,
+seeded from its best timestamps; absent entries never delete v1. Store processed
+legacy payload digest+timestamp in v1. A late old-client edit may contribute LWW
+but cannot erase canonical structure. Never place v1 data in fields/paths that
+old `migrateSched` or `rosterProfile` writes.
 
-`syncV:1` is the marker. First new-client load of state without it assigns one
-`tick()` clock to every extant record (same millisecond, device-id tie breaker),
-creates no tombstones, assigns schedule ids/translates marks, validates, then
-atomically saves local state before its first cloud push. If save fails, retain
-legacy in memory, warn through existing persistent-save warning, and do not
-publish migration. Re-running is idempotent; interruption before the save simply
-restarts; after save recognises `syncV:1`.
+Canonical v1 roster is separate child `{id,ownerUid,c,del}`; do not rely on
+legacy `profiles`. A cloud-roster matching profile silently auto-links to that
+account. A cloud-never-seen `ownerUid:null` profile asks before first upload. An
+A-owned profile cannot upload under B without explicit transfer. Profile delete
+first commits v1 tombstone/cloud child deletion; then removes local state and
+`wardround.bak.<profileId>`. Any cloud/local removal failure is surfaced and
+keeps retryable local data. Sign-out offers removal of that UID's profiles and
+backups and surfaces sign-out/removal failures.
 
-Never delete/rename live or backup `wardround.*` keys. `loadState` retains its
-missing/unparseable-only rescue contract. Old client compatibility is via the
-child canonical document and legacy bridge above; a newer state is not placed
-only in the old whole-state field. An old client may lose its own unsupported
-metadata in legacy state, but cannot remove canonical v1 data; its subsequent
-legacy progress is imported by `legacyAppliedAt`.
+Pin exact Firebase CDN scripts with SHA-384 `integrity` and
+`crossOrigin='anonymous'` before append. Keep `loadSDK()` 8 s and `boot()` 15 s
+local-only fallback.
 
 ## Acceptance checks
 
-| Case | Concrete check | Device requirement |
-|---|---|---|
-| Real auth | Two browser profiles sign into a real test Firebase account, independently edit same/different records, force push/pull; assert record winner/tombstone and UID isolation. | Real network/account |
-| Popup/redirect blocked | Stub popup rejection `popup-blocked`, assert redirect call and retained local gate; standalone path asserts redirect. | iOS standalone redirect needs real iOS Safari |
-| Account switch | A-owned profile under B has no cloud write; unlinked prompt requires explicit Upload; choose Keep and assert no write. | Scriptable with mocked Firebase; real auth smoke |
-| Offline restart | Block network, write, close/reopen; assert local state and backup recovery rules; reconnect then merge. | Scriptable; iOS/Android real smoke |
-| Storage failure | Throw on `setItem`/storage.set; assert warning, no false success, download offered, memory remains usable. | Scriptable |
-| Migration interruption | Seed v0, interrupt before/after local migration save; restart and assert one stable-id mapping/no loss/no duplicate clocks. | Scriptable |
-| SW update | Serve old shell then activate updated worker mid-queued push; reload and assert canonical record/tombstone survives. | Scriptable desktop; real iOS Safari and Android browser/PWA |
+| Case | Expected result / method |
+|---|---|
+| Real auth | Two real test-account browsers: envelope winner, UID isolation, retry. |
+| Blocked popup/redirect | Stub `popup-blocked`; redirect/local gate; real iOS standalone redirect. |
+| Account switch | A cannot write under B; seen roster auto-links; unseen requires choice. |
+| Offline restart | Edit offline, reload/reconnect; local persistence and pull-before-push. Real iOS/Android smoke. |
+| Storage failure | Throw set/remove; persistent warning; no success/deletion claim. |
+| Migration interruption | Interrupt before/after save; one id/clock mapping; no loss. |
+| SW update | Update during queued sync; canonical record/tombstone survives. Desktop scripted; real iOS/Android. |
 
