+## Refuter round 1 — how each defect is closed
+
+| Defect | Doc section |
+|---|---|
+| D1 device identity/clock copied | Isolation and wire format; HLC |
+| D2 migration-time clocks | Validation, migration, ownership |
+| D3 slow clock after merge | HLC, writes, and merge |
+| D4 kinds/schedule/notes incomplete | Isolation; HLC, writes, and merge |
+| D5 legacy state/import/absence | Isolation; Validation, migration, ownership |
+| D6 old-client sched/roster damage | Isolation; Validation, migration, ownership |
+| D7 tombstone horizon/GC | Tombstones and retention |
+| D8 invalid live-state rescue | Evidence; Validation, migration, ownership |
+| D9 nonshippable split | Ordered build split |
+| A offline edit vs B delete | Greater envelope clock wins; retained tombstone wins if greater. |
+| Equal clocks | `deviceId` tie; device-only ids prevent collision. |
+| Device 1 h fast | Fast wins until receive; HLC makes later slow edit win. |
+| Old client after new | Only legacy paths change; v1 survives; present legacy entries import LWW. |
+| Offline >1 year | Pull precedes push; stale absence suppresses local; residual legacy/manual risk disclosed. |
 
