+## Tombstones and retention
 
-Profile delete: first write its roster tombstone and delete cloud profile/sync
-documents in a bounded transaction/batch; only then remove local profile, live
-key, and `wardround.bak.<profileId>`. If cloud delete fails, keep local data and
-show retryable "Cloud profile delete failed"; never toast success. Local storage
-failures are likewise surfaced.
+Every `drop`, including `srs`, `hl`, `flags`, `conf`, `days`, `sched`, schedule
+day/item, notes, profiles, and every other kind writes `del:true`. Retain all
+tombstones one year from winning clock. GC only during successful authenticated
+v1 transaction after remote/local merge; never offline/local-only. Remove only
+expired tombstones from both canonical copies, atomically.
 
