-`tick()` clock to every extant record (same millisecond, device-id tie breaker),
-creates no tombstones, assigns schedule ids/translates marks, validates, then
-atomically saves local state before its first cloud push. If save fails, retain
-legacy in memory, warn through existing persistent-save warning, and do not
-publish migration. Re-running is idempotent; interruption before the save simply
-restarts; after save recognises `syncV:1`.
+Canonical v1 roster is separate child `{id,ownerUid,c,del}`; do not rely on
+legacy `profiles`. A cloud-roster matching profile silently auto-links to that
+account. A cloud-never-seen `ownerUid:null` profile asks before first upload. An
+A-owned profile cannot upload under B without explicit transfer. Profile delete
+first commits v1 tombstone/cloud child deletion; then removes local state and
+`wardround.bak.<profileId>`. Any cloud/local removal failure is surfaced and
+keeps retryable local data. Sign-out offers removal of that UID's profiles and
+backups and surfaces sign-out/removal failures.
 
