+Add device-only key `wardround.sync.device.v1`:
+`{deviceId,lastWall,lastLogical,lastSeenOnlineAt}`. Generate `deviceId` once,
+durable per installation. Never put this key in `S`, cloud, export, import,
+`mergeStates`, or profile copies. This prevents `mergeStates`' clone
+(`gate.js:205`) and import's `Object.assign` (`boot.js:284`) adopting a peer id.
 
-`tick()` returns `[max(Date.now(), S.clock+1), deviceId]`, updates `S.clock`, and
-is called by one `putRecord(k,id,value)` or `deleteRecord(k,id)` helper before
-every `save()`: quiz SRS/conf/flag/highlight writes, all highlight removal, and
-schedule mark/day/item/whole-plan changes. The helper updates both map and
-envelope; delete removes the materialised map entry and writes `del:true`.
-`migrateSched()` must use the helper only after legacy conversion.
+Canonical cloud data is new child `users/{uid}/profiles/{pid}/sync/v1`, holding
+`syncV:1` and `records`; it never uses old profile `state`. After v1 activation,
+new clients read/write only this child and leave legacy `state` untouched: they
+do not write a legacy projection. Old clients may overwrite legacy `state` and
+`profiles`, but cannot write/remove v1 clocks, ownership, or tombstones.
 
-For a record present on both sides, choose lexicographically greatest `c`
-(`wallMs`, then opaque `deviceId` byte order); tombstone is an ordinary winner.
-Thus equal clocks are deterministic in either merge direction. Clocks are
-client wall time, not trusted chronology: a clock behind advances locally via
-`max`; a clock far ahead wins until another write exceeds it. Show one nonfatal
-"device clock differs; latest sync follows its clock" notice per session when
-incoming wall time is >24 h ahead/behind local time; never rewrite received
-clocks. State-level settings retain their current explicit rules unless moved to
-records later.
+`records` has the complete kinds: `answers`, `srs`, `hl`, `flags`, `conf`,
+`days`, `sched`, `scheduleDay`, `scheduleItem`, `notes`, `reports`,
+`resumeByChapter`, `mockResume`, `term`. Entries are
+`{v:<validated existing value>,c:[wall,logical,deviceId],del?:true}`. Missing
+means unknown/no change, never delete; only a winning `del:true` deletes.
+Materialise current `S` shapes after merge; envelopes are canonical.
 
-`schedule` item shape becomes `{id,label,text,hex}`; id is `deviceId + '-' +
-tick()[0]` at creation and is never regenerated. Mark key is `date+'|'+item.id`.
-Render/edit/delete by id, not index. A legacy item gets an id once during
-migration; legacy `date|index` marks are translated in the same in-memory
-transaction. A deleted item records a `sched` tombstone; deleted day/reset
-records tombstones for every contained stable mark/item. Do not renumber.
+## HLC, writes, and merge
 
-Notes join the same envelope/tombstone mechanism (although already individually
-timestamped: `app/js/gate.js:232-242`); highlights are one record per question.
-Profiles use `{id,ownerUid|null,...,c,del?:true}` in a separately merged roster.
-Profile, note, highlight and schedule tombstones live 90 days after their winning
-clock, then GC only during a successful authenticated transaction after merging
-both sides. Never GC offline or local-only; deletion wins throughout retention.
+`issue()` returns `[w,l,deviceId]`: `w=max(Date.now(),lastWall)`; if equal,
+`l=lastLogical+1`, otherwise `l=0`; persist counters before state write. On a
+received `[rw,rl]`, raise local HLC: `lastWall=max(lastWall,rw,Date.now())`; if
+that is `rw`, `lastLogical=max(lastLogical,rl)+1`, otherwise reset/retain for the
+newer local wall. Persist before another edit. Compare lexicographically
+`(wall,logical,deviceId byte order)`; tombstone participates. Equal clocks
+therefore converge deterministically.
 
-## Cloud, validation, ownership
+Clocks order, not chronology. A one-hour-fast device wins records during that
+hour; a later slow-device edit is issued above received maximum and wins. A
+received clock >24 h from local wall gives one non-blocking session warning; do
+not rewrite received clocks.
 
-Extract `parseProgressState(raw)` in `boot.js`: JSON parse then
-`checkedProgressState`; import and every cloud read call this exact function.
-Extend `checkedProgressState` for `syncV`, clock/envelopes/tombstones, stable
-schedule ids, and profile owner fields; preserve unrelated forward fields as it
-does today (`app/js/boot.js:197-264`). Invalid cloud state is not merged or
-written back: set sync error with "Cloud progress was not accepted" and retain
-local state.
+All mutations use `put(kind,id,value)` / `drop(kind,id)`: issue clock, update
+envelope/materialised view, save/debounce. Route every quiz SRS/conf/flag/
+highlight write; every answer/note/report/resume/mock/term write; and every
+schedule write through them. This replaces direct `save()` paths such as
+`setConf`.
 
